*Heading
Simply supported planar beam (B21): natural frequencies and Euler buckling
** L = 1000, RECT section 20 (out of plane, local 1) x 40 (in plane, local 2), E = 210000,
** rho = 7.85e-9.  Euler-Bernoulli: f_n = n^2 pi / (2 L^2) sqrt(E I / (rho A)) = 93.81 and
** 375.25 Hz, buckling load P = pi^2 E I / L^2 = 221079, with the in-plane I = 20 * 40^3 / 12.
** ccx runs B21 as a 3-D B31, so abq2ccx fixes DOF 3 on the beam's nodes (else nothing holds
** it in its plane) and DOFs 4-5 at the pinned end (else the free twist is a 0 Hz mode and
** the buckling factor is meaningless).
